SwiGLU consumes merged gate/up tensors and returns a merged input gradient;
provider dispatch, autotuning and fused-linear orchestration were removed.
python/ctikernels/gdn/_fla.py adapts the forward/backward composition from
fla/ops/gated_delta_rule/chunk.py. python/ctikernels/gdn/triton/_train_{intra,state,output,conv}.py
adapt the chunked gated delta rule's forward and backward kernels (kkt solve, recompute_w_u,
chunk_delta_h, chunk_o's output, dv_local and dqkwg, prepare_wy_repr_bwd, the gate backward)
for K = V = 128 and 64-token chunks: fixed launch configurations, varlen chunk tables, the
reverse cumulative sum and the gate and beta-sigmoid backward fused into the WY backward, and
the q/k L2 norm backward fused into the conv's input gradient. Other provider calls are dependency use.
python/ctikernels/gdn/_fla_fixed.py adapts training host wrappers, preserving
allocations and reductions while launching the original JIT kernels with fixed configs.
python/ctikernels/gdn/_l2norm.py adapts the l2norm_fwd/l2norm_bwd wrappers,
calling the original FLA JIT kernels with a fixed configuration instead of autotuning.
python/ctikernels/gdn/_gated_norm.py adapts layer_norm_gated_bwd_kernel from
fla/modules/fused_norm_gate.py, retaining its products, order and tile shape
while removing weight/bias gradients, residuals, layer-norm/sigmoid variants
and autotuning. The gdn extra pins fla-core 0.5.2.
python/ctikernels/gdn/_fla_training.py adapts the causal conv forward and input
gradient from fla/modules/conv/triton/ops.py and fla/modules/conv/triton/kernels.py,
and gate_gradient's da arithmetic from gdn_gate_bwd in
fla/ops/gated_delta_rule/gate.py, omitting A_log and dt_bias weight gradients.
The local conv kernels write directly into contiguous q/k/v and recompute
pre-activations. Conv backward uses Gluon on NVIDIA GeForce RTX 5090,
NVIDIA RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell Server Edition and NVIDIA GB10; other devices
use Triton. tests/modules/_gdn_training_reference.py restates the same conv
and gate arithmetic from these three upstream paths in PyTorch.
python/ctikernels/gdn/_cute.py restates _fla.py's training composition (from
chunk.py) around the CuTe DSL provider's own chunk kernels on sm_120 / sm_121.
tests/gpu/test_gdn_cute.py restates chunk_gated_delta_rule_bwd's composition of
fla-core's backward kernels as its comparison reference.
python/ctikernels/gdn/_cute_bwd.py's GradQK adapts chunk_bwd_kernel_dqkwg's
organization from fla/ops/common/chunk_o.py: one CTA per key split, chunk and
value head, accumulating over value tiles, a gate-gradient plane per key split
and the last-row correction. Its other kernels, and _cute_fwd.py, implement the
algorithm in CuTe DSL and carry no FLA code.
CUTLASS / CuTe DSL is an external dependency.
